            <div xml:id="d871">

                <pb facs="0870" n="866" sameAs="frus:frus1939v03/pg866"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.51/6995: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in China</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-11-02T13:00:00-05:00">November 2, 1939—1
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>215. Department’s 197, October 19, 8 p.m., foreign personnel of the Chinese
                    Government Salt Administration. It is suggested that the information contained
                    in Shanghai’s despatch no. 2532, September 15, 1939, and its enclosures may be
                    of use in connection with your approaches to the Chinese.</p>
                <p>Sent to Chungking. Repeated to Shanghai.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
